          dealing: 'Each player is dealt 3 cards. The next card is turned up to set the Trump suit. The rest form a draw stock.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Avoid being the last player left with cards in your hand after the stock is exhausted.',
          gameplay: "1. **Lead**: One player leads a card to the 'Play Pile'.\n2. **Response**: The opponent MUST beat the top card (higher of same suit or any Trump). If they beat it, they MUST 'Pile Up' a second card from their hand on top.\n3. **Failure to Beat**: If you cannot beat the card:\n   - If a plain card: Pick up only that card.\n   - If a Trump (not Ace): Pick up the top 3 cards of the pile.\n   - If the Ace of Trumps: Pick up the entire pile.",
          keyRules: [
            'Must beat the top card if possible',
            'After beating, must pile up a second card',
            'Cannot beat: pickup penalty based on card type',
            'Plain card: pickup 1 card',
            'Trump (not Ace): pickup 3 cards',
            'Ace of Trumps: pickup entire pile',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Keep at least one Trump card in reserve (especially the Ace). This is your 'Get out of jail free' card. If you are forced to beat a high card, the Ace guarantees you can move the turn to your opponent.",
          intermediate: 'Pile Management: If the pile is small, intentionally pick up a low plain card rather than using a high card to beat it. This keeps your hand count low and preserves your power cards for when the pile gets dangerous.',
          advanced: "The 'Nakladka' Trap: Bait your opponent into winning a small trick, then use your 'piling up' card to play a mid-range Trump. This forces them into a high-risk situation where they might have to pick up 3 cards, including the trump you just played.",
          tips: [
            "In the 2-player game, memory of the Trumps is fairly easy. Track the 'Ace of Trumps' constantlyâ€”it is the game-winner.",
            'Discard your 6s and 7s of non-trump suits as quickly as possible during the stock-drawing phase.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
